#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""nizho-import: bring your personal files over from a Windows or macOS drive.

    nizho-import scan SOURCE              find what can be imported and print a summary
    nizho-import files SOURCE --dry-run   list exactly what would be copied
    nizho-import files SOURCE             copy it into your home folder
    nizho-import bookmarks SOURCE         write browser bookmarks to one HTML file

SOURCE is a mounted Windows drive (Users/NAME/Documents and so on), a macOS home or
Time Machine style folder (Documents, Pictures, Movies, ...), or any plain folder.
A plain folder is copied into ~/Imported/FOLDERNAME.

The source is only ever read. Nothing in your home folder is overwritten: a name that
already exists with different content keeps both, and the new one is saved as
"name (imported).ext", then "name (imported 2).ext". Identical files are skipped.
Browser profiles, password stores and keychains are not imported.

Bookmarks only: saved passwords, cookies, history and whole profiles are never read.
The bookmarks file goes to ~/Documents/Bookmarks (or --to FILE) and never replaces a file.

Exit code: 0 everything copied, 2 some files were skipped because of an error, 1 fatal error.
"""
